{"name":"Chickweed","hex":"#d9dfe3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chickweed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several small-leaved herbs of the genera Cerastium and Stellaria.\nespecially common chickweed (Stellaria media), a common, edible weed in North America and Europe.\n\nStellaria pro parte\nCerastium (mouse-ear chickweed)","especially common chickweed (Stellaria media), a common, edible weed in North America and Europe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chickweed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stellaria media","blocks":[{"text":"Stellaria media, chickweed, is an annual flowering plant in the family Caryophyllaceae. It is native to Eurasia and naturalized throughout the world, where it is a weed of waste ground, farmland and gardens. It is sometimes grown as a salad crop or for poultry consumption."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Kaldari_Stellaria_media_01.jpg/330px-Kaldari_Stellaria_media_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stellaria_media"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Stellaria_media_stem_hairs.jpg/500px-Stellaria_media_stem_hairs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Stellaria_media_stem_hairs.jpg/1280px-Stellaria_media_stem_hairs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Stellaria_media_stem_hairs.jpg/500px-Stellaria_media_stem_hairs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chickweeds have a line of hairs along one side of stem.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStellaria_media_stem_hairs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Stellaria_Media_%28Common_Chickwe